{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791134483,"nonce":"9sQNKkj9opVPi6mbq7eyDPsOACk=","title":"hxx: event callbacks as attributes on every element, bound to its Interaction","message":"Binding an event today means leaving the template: `Interaction.of(el.node).onClick(...)` after the element is built, with a `var` to reach it. Only `\u003ca\u003e` takes `onClick` as an attribute. Form controls take their own value callbacks (`onInput`, `onChange`, `onSubmit`), and `\u003cdiv\u003e`, which every element is built on, takes none.\n\nWanted: the events `Interaction` binds, as typed attributes on every built-in element and on every component, bound to the element's Interaction when it is built:\n\n    \u003cdiv onClick={_ -\u003e save()} onPointerEnter={_ -\u003e hovered.set(true)} onPointerLeave={_ -\u003e hovered.set(false)} focusable={true}\u003e\n    \u003ccard onKeyDown={e -\u003e if (e.key == Named(Escape)) close()}\u003e\n\n- The set: onClick, onPointerDown, onPointerUp, onPointerMove, onPointerEnter, onPointerLeave, onWheel, onKeyDown, onKeyUp, onTextInput, onComposition, onFocus and onBlur, each typed as the Interaction method it binds to (PointerEvent-\u003eVoid and so on). Plus `focusable:Bool` and `disabled:IntoReactive\u003cBool\u003e`, from setFocusable and setDisabled.\n- In DivAttributes, so every element built on Div has them. On a component, hxx binds them to the component's element, since a component is its element, unless the component declares a prop of that name.\n- Where a component or control already declares one with its own meaning, such as Input's `onInput:String-\u003eVoid` (the new value, not the raw text event), the declared prop wins. Then the raw event is still reached through query or Interaction. Write down which names are taken this way, so the two meanings never meet silently.\n- Bound under the element's owner, so the handlers go when it does.\n- An attribute binds when the element is built and once. `query` (git-bug 8ec2dd92badf89667b535f6feda2c1df93e9b4668951efc8ae008b902c8bee53) and refs (git-bug 61d88ace21edc980e28774d06a4423ccdd231c047993651e00fc5a00535a7402) are for binding from code later, or conditionally.\n\nComponents in components/ would then bind in their templates instead of after them, and many of the 46 files calling `Interaction.of` shrink.","files":null}]}